Package: timestralR
Type: Package
Title: Zero-Shot Probabilistic Forecasting with Timestral
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Stefan", "Janse van Rensburg", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "sjansevanrensburg@gmail.com"),
    person("Mistral AI", role = "cph",
           comment = "authors of the 'timestral' Python package ported in R/ and src/"))
URL: https://github.com/sjvrensburg/timestralR
BugReports: https://github.com/sjvrensburg/timestralR/issues
Description: Runs Mistral AI's Timestral time-series foundation models from R
    without Python or PyTorch. The official 'safetensors' checkpoints are
    downloaded once from the Mistral AI Hugging Face repositories; the
    transformer forward pass and the forecasting loop are implemented
    natively in R on top of R's BLAS.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: jsonlite, digest, utils, tools, stats, Rcpp (>= 1.0.0)
Suggests: zoo, xts, tsibble, ggplot2, fabletools, distributional,
    tidyselect, fable, rlang, knitr, rmarkdown, patchwork, dplyr, feasts,
    ggtime, forecast
VignetteBuilder: knitr
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen
SystemRequirements: A C++17 compiler. Model weights are downloaded on
    first use from huggingface.co (Mistral AI, Modified MIT licence).
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
